supplier_support.claim:
Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice, written $\mathrm{AC}_\omega$, and let $n\ge2$. Let $\Omega\subset\mathbb R^n$ be a bounded $C^1$ domain carrying a Dirichlet Green function $G_\Omega$ for $-\Delta$. For every pole $p\in\Omega$, assume its designated corrector satisfies $H_p\in C^2(\overline\Omega)$, as required by the Green-symmetry hypothesis. For $x\in\Omega$ and $y\in\partial\Omega$, define the boundary-slot normal derivative by $$\partial_{
u_y}G_\Omega(x,y):=D_z igl(\Phi(z-x)-H_x(z) igr) ig|_{z=y}\cdot
u_\Omega(y),$$ and define the Poisson kernel by $$P_\Omega(x,y):=-\partial_{
u_y}G_\Omega(x,y).$$ Here $\Phi$ is the positive-minus-Laplacian fundamental solution fixed in [[def-dirichlet-green-function-for-minus-laplacian]],…

